  "title": "Stash Alternatives 2026: Pricing and Features Compared",
  "h1": "Stash Alternatives 2026: Pricing and Features Compared",
  "metaDescription": "Stash alternatives compared: Acorns, Betterment, Wealthfront, Robinhood, M1 and Fidelity Go, with published monthly fees, advisory rates and retirement matches.",
  "published": "2026-11-20",
  "updated": "2026-11-20",
  "intro": "Acorns, Betterment, Wealthfront, Robinhood, M1 and Fidelity Go are six Stash alternatives. They charge in three ways: a flat monthly fee, a percentage of assets, or no advisory fee at all. The cheaper pick depends on account size and on extras such as an individual retirement account (IRA) match, a cash annual percentage yield (APY) or banking.\n\n[Stash](https://www.stash.com/pricing) sells one plan, The Stash Plan, at $12 per month or $108 billed annually, which Stash lists as a 25% saving. Stash also charges an assets under management (AUM) advisory fee of 0.25% a year on Smart Portfolios with balances of $1,000 or more and on Managed Retirement Accounts. The plan includes a 3% retirement match worth up to $225 per year, a $10,000 life insurance policy and Stock-Back rewards worth up to $120 per year.\n\nThe table lists each provider's published prices, and the sections below turn those prices into yearly costs at set balances. For related shortlists, see the [Acorns alternatives](/alternatives/acorns/) guide, the [best robo-advisors roundup](/roundup/best-robo-advisors/) and the [guide to what brokers charge to trade](/guides/what-do-brokers-charge-to-trade/). The [comparison hub](/compare/) holds wider money software breakdowns.",
